{{!
    @template tool_vae/consent_page

    The page "Accord pour annoter", below its heading: what the consent is, the people who may receive it with the state of
    each (or one sentence when there is nobody), the dated history, and the way back to the dossier.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\consent_page. The template holds no logic. Every
    text and address is escaped (double braces), except one key of HTML made by another template (triple braces):
    tablehtml, a table drawn by the template tool_vae/table (the names and states in it are escaped by the template
    tool_vae/cell_content; the buttons are made by the core).

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * intro - string, what the consent is
    * none - false, or a string: the sentence drawn when nobody may receive the consent
    * tablehtml - false, or HTML: the table of the people
    * history - false, or {label, tablehtml}: the heading and the table of the history
    * back - {url, label}: the way back to the dossier

    Example context (json):
    {
        "intro": "You may allow a manager who follows you to annotate your dossier. You may take it back at any time.",
        "none": false,
        "tablehtml": "<table class=\"generaltable\"><tbody><tr><td>Marie Lefèvre</td><td>Given</td></tr></tbody></table>",
        "history": {
            "label": "History of the consent",
            "tablehtml": "<table class=\"generaltable\"><tbody><tr><td>Given</td></tr></tbody></table>"
        },
        "back": {"url": "https://example.com/admin/tool/vae/dossier.php?userid=7", "label": "Back to the dossier"}
    }
}}
<p>{{intro}}</p>
{{#none}}
<p>{{none}}</p>
{{/none}}
{{#tablehtml}}
{{{tablehtml}}}
{{/tablehtml}}
{{#history}}
<h3>{{label}}</h3>
{{{tablehtml}}}
{{/history}}
{{#back}}
<p><a href="{{url}}">{{label}}</a></p>
{{/back}}
